= Introduction

This book contains the 172 drills of A. N. Palmer's _The Palmer Method of
Business Writing_, set out as a practice notebook. Its
companion, the lesson book, reprints Palmer's opening instructions on
position, movement, and penholding and lists the drills to practice in
each lesson.

== Handwriting Examples

The handwriting plates from the original book have been reproduced here, 
straightened and scaled so that they match Palmer's recommended x-height of
one-sixteenth of an inch. The slant guide lines are set at 55 degrees as a reference only; Palmer asks for uniform slant rather than any particular angle. The cross-line
drills are reproduced at full size without ruling.

== Daily drills

A star after a drill number marks a drill to practice
at the beginning of every lesson. These drills, with Drills 33 and 169 and
the speed chart from the original, are also printed as a separate sheet of
daily drills for easy printing.

== The text

The instructions are those from the original book, lightly copyedited. Notes addressed to
teachers, references to the original's page numbers, and the maxims printed
at the foot of its pages have been left out. The division of the drills into
lessons, and the instructions given between drills, are available in the
lesson book.

== Printing

This book is set for printing on A5 paper. The
50 mm bar at the foot of each page allows checking that the book was printed at
correct size; if it does not measure 50 mm, the letters will not be their intended
size.

